        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]}
      ],
      "budget_share": 0.5,
      "why": "iterative is the lowest-power family (one shared datapath, no per-stage registers). The 50 MSPS throughput constraint forces Fmax >= 50 MHz, which is easily met by the short critical path of a single micro-rotation. The accuracy constraint (max_abs_err <= 2^-12) requires data_width >= 14 and n_iter >= 12; I narrow the ranges to the feasible band to focus the search on the power/accuracy trade-off rather than wasting evals on infeasible or grossly over-accurate corners."
    },
    {
      "family": "unrolled_k",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 14, "high": 18, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 12, "high": 16, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": 0, "high": 2, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 2, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]},
        {"param": "k", "low": 2, "high": 4, "choices": null}
      ],
      "budget_share": 0.5,
      "why": "unrolled_k chains k micro-rotations per cycle, reducing latency and potentially allowing a slightly lower Fmax for the same throughput, but at the cost of a longer combinational path and more area/power. With k=2..4 and N=12..16, the critical path stays short enough for 50+ MHz. This family may find a lower-power point if the reduced clock frequency (due to higher throughput per cycle) outweighs the added logic. I cap k at 4 to keep the critical path manageable in sky130."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The spec requires 50 MSPS throughput and max_abs_err <= 2^-12, minimising power_index. Both iterative and unrolled_k are the only families available to me, and both can plausibly meet the constraints. The accuracy constraint pins data_width >= 14 (since output LSB is 2^-(W-2), we need W-2 >= 12) and n_iter >= 12 for sufficient convergence. I narrow the search to data_width 14-18 and n_iter 12-16 to focus on the feasible trade-off region. The throughput constraint (>= 50 MSPS) is easily met by both families at typical Fmax values. I split the budget 50/50 between the two families to map the Pareto front across both, since unrolled_k may offer a different power/accuracy trade-off due to its higher throughput per cycle and different critical path structure. The angle_guard and frac_guard ranges are kept tight (0-2) since larger values add area/power without meaningful accuracy benefit in this range."
}

